WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.279
Big new releases seem few and far between
these days, but there’s still plenty to

00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:08.050
play, especially if you’ve got Xbox Game
Pass.

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:18.640
Here are 8 games to check out if you’re
subscribed to Microsoft's service.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:23.350
Life is Strange: True Colors, the latest in
the choice-driven episodic adventure series

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:26.269
from Square Enix is finally on Game Pass.

00:00:26.269 --> 00:00:32.840
You play as Alex Chen, who moves to the sleepy
town of Haven Springs to start a new life,

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:35.570
only to be beset with tragedy when she gets
there.

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:40.580
With the help of her newfound friends Steph
and Ryan, she’s determined to figure out

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:43.540
what’s really going on in Haven Springs.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:47.120
Helping in this quest is her power: Empathy.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:52.420
Alex can sense and even manipulate the strong
feelings of others, and in True Colors, she

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:57.830
uses it to help the townsfolk of Haven Springs
in many memorable and beautiful ways; from

00:00:57.830 --> 00:01:02.930
a woman struggling with keeping a secret from
her granddaughter, to an unlucky kid with

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:05.229
an overactive imagination.

00:01:05.229 --> 00:01:10.210
Just like previous Life is Strange games,
True Colors offers a fantastic indie soundtrack

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:16.650
including the likes of Radiohead, Phoebe Bridgers,
and mxmtoon, but beware if you’re streaming

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:25.479
it because… well, let’s just say streamer
mode really takes the mood out of the moment.

00:01:25.479 --> 00:01:34.659
But don’t let that discourage you, Life
is Strange: True Colors is a truly heartfelt

00:01:34.659 --> 00:01:40.020
and emotional rollercoaster, and as all episodes
come in one package, you’ll probably find

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:52.829
yourself playing all 5 in rapid succession
to get to the bottom of the mystery that lies

00:01:52.829 --> 00:01:53.961
at its heart.

00:01:53.961 --> 00:01:59.960
Bugsnax is a delightfully bizarre puzzle adventure
game from the team behind Octodad: Dadliest

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:00.960
Catch.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:05.979
Originally a timed PlayStation exclusive,
the game is finally making its way to other

00:02:05.979 --> 00:02:09.360
platforms, and is creeping onto Xbox Game
Pass.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:15.010
You play as an investigative journalist invited
to the mysterious Snaktooth Island by intrepid

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:20.470
explorer Elizabert Megafig… but when you
arrive, you find she’s gone missing under

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:22.660
suspicious circumstances.

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:28.380
Even weirder are the island’s local fauna,
the eponymous Bugsnax.

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:33.770
Half animal, half… delicious snack, it’s
up to you to scour the land, uncover all the

00:02:33.770 --> 00:02:38.390
species, and capture the creatures to solve
the mysteries of Snaktooth Island.

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:43.720
Bugsnax is as adorable as it is zany, and
definitely one that will scratch the Gotta

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:46.520
Catch ‘Em All itch of Pokemon fans.

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:53.650
It does get a little dark as you need to catch
the cutesy Bugsnax and then, er, feed them

00:02:53.650 --> 00:03:01.200
to the residents of Snaktooth Isle, but with
a theme song this catchy from Kero Kero Bonito,

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:06.500
who could say no.

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:11.620
Young Horses also recently launched a free
expansion for Bugsnax owners called The Isle

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:14.370
Of Bigsnax, where the Bugsnax are…

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:18.160
well, I’m sure you can guess.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:23.980
Are you in the mood for a cozy single player
adventure game about an adorable turnip…

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:25.450
who commits CRIMES?

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:31.760
Well, if that very specific mood strikes you,
Turnip Boy Commits Tax Evasion is just the

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:32.820
game for you.

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:39.260
It launched on Steam in 2021 to thousands
of Very Positive user reviews, and now this

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:45.560
cute menace, I mean seriously, look at their
little face, is making their way to Game Pass.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:50.790
You start the game by being evicted from your
home for failing to pay your taxes.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:55.510
Burdened with debt and under the thumb of
Mayor Onion, you head out into the world to

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:57.000
pay back what you owe.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:02.220
Along the way, you solve puzzles, traverse
dungeons, defeat enemies, solve problems for

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:07.910
others, hunt for treasure, and of course,
rip up tax documents to erase your paper trail.

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:14.360
See, not all is as it seems, and there’s
a corrupt government and capitalist pigs to

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:15.360
take down.

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:19.069
The ending of the game depends on just how
good you are at committing and getting away

00:04:19.069 --> 00:04:22.990
with tax evasion, so keep that in mind as
you play.

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:27.639
Oh, and did I mention there are hats to collect
and wear?

00:04:27.639 --> 00:04:29.540
Very important.

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:32.610
Okay, so far these selections have been very
wholesome…

00:04:32.610 --> 00:04:38.060
sort of… so let’s completely 180 that
with 7 Days To Die.

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:44.039
This zombie title is a true mix of gameplay
genres, part first-person shooter, part tower

00:04:44.039 --> 00:04:47.879
defense, part RPG, and part survival horror.

00:04:47.879 --> 00:04:54.240
Developer The Fun Pimps launched 7 Days to
Die back in 2013 via Steam Early Access, and

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:57.370
now it’s making its way to Xbox Game Pass.

00:04:57.370 --> 00:05:01.879
Following a nuclear war that destroyed much
of the world and left it overrun by zombies,

00:05:01.879 --> 00:05:03.810
it’s up to you to explore and survive.

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:04.810
Either working cooperatively or alone, you
can build bases, raid settlements, farm, hunt,

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:05.810
craft, loot, drive, kill zombies [intake of
breath].

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:08.120
Yeah, there’s a lot to get to grips with,
but don’t be discouraged, there are years

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:18.800
of fan wikis and a dedicated community ready
to guide you through.

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:21.810
Wanna solve crimes from the safety of your
living room?

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:27.289
Try out Chinatown Detective Agency, a point
and click adventure game with a twist.

00:05:27.289 --> 00:05:33.220
You play as Amira Darma, an ex-INTERPOL cop
who has set up her own private detective agency.

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:38.969
As Amira you get to travel around the futuristic,
neon-infused world to meet clients and solve

00:05:38.969 --> 00:05:43.660
their cases, but it’s not as simple as just
solving crimes: you’ve got to make sure

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:49.159
your agency remains in the black and budget
for things like expansion and hiring staff.

00:05:49.159 --> 00:05:53.960
When it comes to doing actual detective work,
Chinatown Detective Agency requires you to

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:59.860
do your own research, so yes, that can mean
firing up Google to search for answers, or

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:02.599
asking the in-game librarian Mei for help.

00:06:02.599 --> 00:06:08.069
If a gritty noir detective game sounds up
your street, then this is the one for you.

00:06:08.069 --> 00:06:13.580
If you have Game Pass Ultimate or EA Play,
then here’s a couple that you should take

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:21.309
a look at, first up is Lost in Random, which
is described by publisher EA as “a gothic-fairy-tale-inspired

00:06:21.309 --> 00:06:25.949
action-adventure where every citizen's fate
is determined by the roll of a dice”.

00:06:25.949 --> 00:06:29.650
I can’t really summarize it more succinctly
than that, so there you have it.

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:34.659
If you’re interested in the premise, the
game was written by Ryan North, who you might

00:06:34.659 --> 00:06:38.000
recognise as the author of the Unbeatable
Squirrel Girl.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:43.020
Playing as a girl named Even and joined by
her dice pal Dicey, your quest is to save

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:48.120
your sister, but the odds are stacked against
you: in the Kingdom of Random, a wicked Queen

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:50.620
with a cursed black dice runs the show.

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:56.100
The gameplay is a mix of card collecting and
tactical combat, all set in gorgeous and twisted

00:06:56.100 --> 00:07:01.919
board games, where the world definitely has
a touch of the Tim Burtons about it.

00:07:01.919 --> 00:07:06.990
Another one for EA Play and Game Pass Ultimate
subscribers, but Dragon Age 2 has finally

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:07.990
made it to Game Pass.

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:11.469
I know what you’re going to say: there’s
a lot wrong with Dragon Age 2.

00:07:11.469 --> 00:07:18.740
Yes, it uses the same environments way, way
too many times, yes it was clearly made in

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:24.130
a bit of a rush and lost a lot of the deep
RPG-ness of Dragon Age Origins, but… is

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:25.440
it still a fun romp?

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:26.440
Yes.

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:30.139
Is it less clunky and more action packed than
the first game?

00:07:30.139 --> 00:07:31.139
Also yes.

00:07:31.139 --> 00:07:35.030
If like me, you’re twiddling your thumbs
waiting for the next Dragon Age, instead of

00:07:35.030 --> 00:07:39.949
replaying Inquisition again–look, we’ve
all been there–why not give Dragon Age 2

00:07:39.949 --> 00:07:41.469
another chance.

00:07:41.469 --> 00:07:46.379
Okay, secretly I'm not even sure when this
one got put on Game Pass, but Kurt’s not

00:07:46.379 --> 00:07:51.409
here to tell me no, so we’re gonna round
off this episode by recommending Alan Wake’s

00:07:51.409 --> 00:07:52.669
American Nightmare.

00:07:52.669 --> 00:07:57.389
This standalone spin-off to 2010’s Alan
Wake follows our beleaguered best-selling

00:07:57.389 --> 00:08:01.990
author as he comes up against his biggest
foe yet: himself.

00:08:01.990 --> 00:08:07.129
Or rather, the purely evil version of himself
known as Mr Scratch.

00:08:07.129 --> 00:08:12.180
American Nightmare definitely leans more into
more pulpy horror tropes than the original

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:17.380
did, and even added a new arcade mode, essentially
a horde mode where players can battle for

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:21.879
the top spot on leaderboards after they face
waves of enemies.

00:08:21.879 --> 00:08:27.240
Since Alan Wake 2's development has finally
been confirmed by Remedy, now really is the

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:32.430
time to go back and play his first couple
of adventures, and if you’ve got the time,

00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:37.229
definitely hit up the AWE expansion for Control
to get the full story.

00:08:37.229 --> 00:08:42.959
So there you have it, the best games to play
on Xbox Game Pass this month, make sure to

00:08:42.959 --> 00:08:46.790
let me know your favorites in the comments
below, and let me know how you get on with

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:47.800
what I’ve recommended.

00:08:47.800 --> 00:09:00.600
I’m on Twitter @lucyjamesgames, see ya next
time.

